Adjudicated at rank 1 before the comment fix: read evalPosition
(metal_runtime_darwin.go:517) and EvalBatch (:561). evalPosition returns
early at 'if !logits' before the output projection, and EvalBatch passes
logits=true only at i == len(tokens)-1. So the head runs once per
EvalBatch, not once per token, and a 32-token prefill chunk is
32*86 + 1 = 2753 spans. The 87-per-token figure the head fix was
adjudicated against is the decode path, where every Eval is its own
last position.

